  "description": "You quit a Wall Street job to sell books on the internet. It's 1994.\n\nSources:\n- Wikipedia: Jeff Bezos: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jeff_Bezos\n- Wikipedia: Amazon (company): https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazon_(company)\n\nFrom the cited pages: Bezos worked at D. E. Shaw from 1990 to 1994 and left to found Amazon; the business plan was written on a cross-country drive from New York City to Seattle; Amazon was founded in a rented garage in Bellevue, Washington, on July 5, 1994, and began as an online bookstore; its IPO three years later made Bezos a millionaire (1997); in 2002 he led Amazon to launch Amazon Web Services; in November 2007 he launched the Kindle; Amazon bought Whole Foods for $13.7 billion on August 28, 2017; Bezos founded Blue Origin in September 2000 and flew on its New Shepard NS-16 flight on July 20, 2021, to 66.5 miles; Amazon revenue was $716.9 billion in 2025 with 1,576,000 employees. Not financial advice.\n\n#shorts #amazon #jeffbezos #howtheymakemoney",
